  "title": "Request processors started at NEWLEADER are not shut down when synchronization fails before UPTODATE",
  "cause": "startupWithoutServing starts the processors but leaves state INITIAL; LearnerZooKeeperServer.shutdown returns early because canShutdown() is false.",
  "trigger": "Any learner failure between NEWLEADER and startServing (e.g. CR-1 or the read timeout injected by DIFFSyncConsistencyTest).",
  "consequence": "Leaked FollowerRequestProcessor/CommitProcessor/RequestThrottler threads; the orphaned SyncThread keeps flushing and dies with a critical-thread error writing to the closed learner socket.",
  "sites": [
    "Learner.java:syncWithLeader zk.startupWithoutServing",
    "ZooKeeperServer.java:canShutdown",
    "LearnerZooKeeperServer.java:shutdown"
  ],
  "actions": [],
  "invariants": [],
  "premises": [
    "A learner can fail after NEWLEADER and before startServing."
  ],
